 that group (scripts/data/nhl-seasons.json computed.histograms: forwards 433, defenders 236, goalies 64); ties stay ties and nobody passes anybody in a group. A player outside the squads takes the rating of the highest squad value in his group not above his. Then every club is moved toward its real results: S is each club's goal differential a game from the Hockey Databank's Teams.csv (a shoot-out's goal taken off both sides; × (n − 1) ÷ n, a club meeting the other n − 1), its reliability from Poisson goals, reliability r 0.702; m, the match model's margin a game per point of a lineup's played strength (the mean of its attack and defence) under the season's rules, is 0.2867 goals (at scoring 0.9222); each club's target is the clubs' mean before the move + √r × S ÷ m, and every player of the club moves by one whole number, its best few one point more, whichever brings its lineup nearest the target (no player passes one rated above him in his club). Every player's lines and the season's results are in scripts/data/nhl-seasons/nhl-1968.json.","licence":"free use of the data, a commercial product included, with the Hockey Databank's attribution statement displayed in its entirety (its readme)","attribution":"The information used herein was obtained free of charge from and is copyrighted by the Hockey Databank project.  For more information about the Hockey Databank project please visit http://sports.groups.yahoo.com/group/hockey-databank","nation":"the Hockey Databank's birth country (a birth it gives in the USSR, Czechoslovakia or Yugoslavia counts for the country the birth city is in today)"},"map":"nhl1968","nations":{},"clubs":[{"id":"nhl-montreal-canadiens","name":"Montreal Canadiens","code":"MTL","league":"NHL","country":"124","col":"oklch(0.72 0.16 317)","str":85.9,"squad":[["Jean Beliveau","C",94],["Henri Richard","C",88],["Ralph Backstrom","C",87],["Jacques Lemaire","C",86],["Gilles Tremblay","LW",88],["Dick Duff","LW",87],["John Ferguson","LW",84],["Danny Gran